Newer mingw-w64 headers declare _utime() with struct _utimbuf *, which is a
distinct type from struct utimbuf (the CTYPE of CUtimbuf). Clang treats the
mismatch in the capi wrapper as an error. The POSIX-named utime() takes
struct utimbuf * and resolves to the same _utime64 import.

--- a/libraries/ghc-internal/src/GHC/Internal/System/Posix/Internals.hs
+++ b/libraries/ghc-internal/src/GHC/Internal/System/Posix/Internals.hs
@@ -729,7 +729,7 @@
 foreign import capi unsafe "HsBase.h _unlink"
    c_unlink :: CString -> IO CInt
 
-foreign import capi unsafe "HsBase.h _utime"
+foreign import capi unsafe "HsBase.h utime"
    c_utime :: CString -> Ptr CUtimbuf -> IO CInt
 
 foreign import capi unsafe "HsBase.h _getpid"
